   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to municipal\nsustainable energy loan programs",
    "basePrintNo": "S6523",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6523-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 40,
       "fullName": "Pete Harckham",
       "imgName": "1053_Pete_Harckham.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1233,
       "sessionMemberId": 1231,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "HARCKHAM"
      },
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 37,
       "fullName": "Shelley Mayer",
       "imgName": "623_shelley_mayer.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1143,
       "sessionMemberId": 1210,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "MAYER"
      }
     ],
     "size": 2
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§119-ff & 119-gg, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6523\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the general municipal law, in relation\nto municipal sustainable energy loan programs\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation will allow sustainable energy loan programs as author-\nized by the general municipal law to be used for new construction.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSections 1 and 2: Amends the general municipal law to update Article 5-L\nto  allow  sustainable  energy  loan  programs  to  be  utilized for new\nconstruction.\n\nSection 3: The effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, general municipal law  allows  for  sustainable  energy  loan\nprograms  that could significantly increase the adoption of clean energy\nby property owners while helping to achieve New York  State's  renewable\nenergy  and  energy  efficiency goals. Similar to how sidewalks, sewers,\nwater systems and other local public projects are financed  via  assess-\nments  or  charges  placed on improved property, sustainable energy loan\nprograms facilitate the improvement of property with lowered  pollution,\nreduced carbon emissions, and lowered energy costs. These investments in\nturn improve the local community by revitalizing buildings and advancing\na  clean  energy  economy.  In  its  current form, general municipal law\ndenies these benefits to new construction. Often times  the  latest  and\nmost  efficient  equipment is sacrificed to keep up-front costs of a new\nconstruction project low. This has the effect of passing on the  result-\ning  higher  costs  of energy, emissions, and pollution to future owners\nand the wider community. Amending the general municipal  law  to  permit\nfinancing  for  energy  related  improvements  in  new construction will\nenable property owners and the professionals  involved  with  designing,\nengineering,  and  constructing  the  new  building stock of New York to\nincorporate the most efficient equipment and  infrastructure.  Moreover,\nimplementing  such  measures  in  new construction will accelerate their\nincorporation into retrofit and rehabilitation projects as  technologies\nare  proven  and  achieve  scale.  This  amendment will directly support\nreducing the future direct and indirect costs of the use of energy while\nsupporting the stated goals and policy of the existing statute.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
